From 0a7f4de4b49219e59a87fc34cb35fb401ae586ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:40:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: an image fetched again is shown again

`reload_resource_by_href` fetched again only the stylesheets linked from
the href, and inline SVG images. An `<img>`, a `background-image` or a
`mask-image` layer kept the image it had: the image cache answered for
the URL, so an embedder whose resource changed (a resource sent again,
a dev server's rebuild) had the old pixels, and an `<img>` the old size.

The image at the href is now dropped from the cache and fetched again,
with every `<img>` that shows it and every background and mask layer
that names it waiting for it, as they do for a first load. An `<img>`
is laid out again when it arrives. An image still on its way is left to
arrive.
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs | 118 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 116 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

